Q: How do I pass props to a function component in TypeScript? I am receiving an error that it&#39;s type is not a valid JSX element type A: <p>A React component only takes a single parameter (the props). It's a complex object holding all properties.</p>
<p>You have a function which accepts two parameters (the constituents of the props):</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function MobileHeader(activeHeader: boolean, activeMenu: boolean) {
  // …
}
</code></pre>
<p>Instead, you want to pass the props directly:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>interface MobileHeaderProps {
  activeHeader: boolean;
  activeMenu: boolean;
} 

function MobileHeader(props: MobileHeaderProps) {
  // …
}
</code></pre>
<p>or destructure directly in the function definition:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>interface MobileHeaderProps {
  activeHeader: boolean;
  activeMenu: boolean;
} 

function MobileHeader({activeHeader, activeMenu}: MobileHeaderProps) {
  // …
}
</code></pre>
<p>See the <a href="https://react.dev/learn/tutorial-tic-tac-toe#passing-data-through-props" rel="nofollow noreferrer">official React tutorial on passing props</a>.</p>
